# Normalise line endings on checkout everywhere.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the common `core.autocrlf=true` gets
# every file as CRLF. That silently breaks needle searches written against the
# committed bytes — `HANDOVER.md` §5.1's client-factory check looks for
# `'},\n})'` and finds nothing at all on a CRLF checkout, reporting a parse
# failure for a file that is perfectly fine.
#
# Text stays LF in the working tree on every platform; only the checkout is
# normalised, so the diff of any future change stays readable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.crx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Windows-only helpers keep CRLF so they stay double-clickable and work with
# cmd.exe / PowerShell 5.1, which both tolerate CRLF better than bare LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
